# Security — Fullstack

## Secrets & Config
- Never commit `.env`, credentials, or tokens
- Sensitive config via environment variables or server-side only

## Input/Output
- Server: validate with an explicit schema (allowlist fields and types); client validation is UX only
- Never use `eval()`, `new Function()`, or dynamic code execution
- Prefer `textContent` over `innerHTML`; sanitize with DOMPurify if `innerHTML` is required
- Never log sensitive data, secrets, or session tokens in application logs
- Links with `target="_blank"` require `rel="noopener noreferrer"`

## Frontend
- Session tokens in `httpOnly` `Secure` `SameSite` cookies — never `localStorage`
- CSRF: classic forms include a hidden token validated server-side; `fetch` mutations use `SameSite` cookies plus a custom header (e.g. `X-Requested-With`) validated server-side
- Content Security Policy via server headers or meta tag
- Escape output in HTML context

## Backend & Data
- Parameterized queries / ORM only; no string concatenation for SQL
- Least-privilege DB users; RBAC for sensitive operations
- Use established auth solutions; do not roll custom crypto
- Store passwords using strong, salted hashes (e.g., Argon2, bcrypt)

## Dependencies & CI
- No new dependencies without approval
- Only use packages from verified sources
- SCA, SAST, and secret scanning in CI pipeline
- Integrate DAST in CD pipeline for deployed applications
- Keep dependencies updated; document security decisions

## Compliance
- Controls in this file cover relevant OWASP Top 10 items for code review; NIST/ISO audit documentation is out of scope for day-to-day reviews
